course: dictionary
lesson: 4706
title: Honeysuckle, a climbing plant
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A honeysuckle is a climbing plant. It twists up walls, fences and hedges, and it has tube-shaped flowers in yellow, white or pink.
explain: The flowers smell sweet and hold nectar, a sugary liquid. Look at this sentence: «Evening primrose and honeysuckle open in the evening with pale petals, which show up best in dim light, and a strong scent.» The clues show that honeysuckle has a strong scent and opens in the evening.
explain: Bees, butterflies and moths come to honeysuckle to drink the nectar. As they move from flower to flower, they carry pollen, which helps new seeds to grow. Context clue: in «the scent of honeysuckle», scent is a smell, so honeysuckle is something that smells.
fact: Honeysuckle is a noun. You can have one honeysuckle or two honeysuckles.
fact: «Honeysuckle» means a climbing plant with sweet-smelling flowers.
fact: Honeysuckle flowers can be yellow, white or pink, and they are tube-shaped.
fact: Nectar is the sweet liquid inside a flower that attracts bees, butterflies and moths.
fact: In poems and stories, honeysuckle is often a symbol of summer evenings. Only pick or taste flowers with a grown-up's permission, and never eat the berries.
exercise: «The honeysuckle hedge filled the garden with its sweet scent.» What does scent mean here? | A colour | A sound | *A smell | A taste
exercise: What is a honeysuckle? | *A climbing plant with sweet-smelling flowers | A kind of stone used to build walls | A small bird that sings at night
exercise: Which visitors drink the nectar from honeysuckle flowers? | Worms and snails | *Bees, butterflies and moths | Sharks and whales | Cows and horses
test: What sweet liquid is found inside honeysuckle flowers? | *Nectar | Salt water | Vinegar | Mud
test: Which word fits the gap? «The climbing ___ covered the fence with pink and white flowers.» | Puddle | *Honeysuckle | Oak | Gravel
exam: Which statement about honeysuckle is correct? | It only grows in deserts | *It is a climbing plant with sweet-smelling, tube-shaped flowers | It is a fish that lives in ponds | It is a stone used to build walls
